      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Slicing is not limited to 5G.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "122734d0_cc6fac07",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ApplicationNetworkSliceCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Our solution being more general than just slicing, I think we should generally avoid the words \"slice\" and \"slicing\", and instead speak in terms of capabilities. Note how nothing in the tree today is calling any of this functionality \"slices\".\n\nSuggest something like :\n\n    ...an immutable class that contains the application properties declared\n    in its manifest about the capabilities that need declaration.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "383a63cb_9b499ae9",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ApplicationNetworkSliceCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Likewise, here let\u0027s not use the \"slice\" term. These are network capabilities.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e62b252_0b7edc90",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ApplicationNetworkSliceCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because this tag may contain multiple capabilities, I suggest we use `network-capabilities-declaration` or similar.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02744ecc_ee0103b1",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ApplicationNetworkSliceCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For permissions we\u0027re using \"uses-permission\". How about \"uses-network-capability\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d802ea12_29fddfa8",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ApplicationNetworkSliceCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If they are invalid, then UOE doesn\u0027t sound like the correct exception – IllegalArgumentException sounds like the right one.\n\nFor incompatibility, that depends what the incompatibility is, but sure – if it\u0027s something that\u0027s not supported then UOE sounds right.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 83,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "5376724bff9c30ee3c01fdf590b4249cd01e0f73",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
