      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T08:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the right way to do this is to define a compat change. You can find an example of this in LinkProperties#EXCLUDED_ROUTES ; the gist of it is you declare a long which corresponds to a bug ID (which enforces unicity) and a policy (@EnabledAfter(UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE)), and then you query it.\n\nThis has the same effect as the code you wrote, but :\n• The developers can turn it on/off on their development device to see if that\u0027s what\u0027s causing their issue and other debugging purposes\n• It gets put in the release notes",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6938,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 6938,
        "endChar": 30
      },
